cast: chidi

== street | EVENING · EUROPEAN STREET | European city street at evening with old buildings, trams and warm lights | stand
chidi (think): Quddus, I heard Germany lets people come without a job offer. Is that a rumour from my uncle's WhatsApp group?
quddus (talk): This one is real. It's called the Opportunity Card, or Chancenkarte. It's a residence permit to look for a job in Germany.
> 1f1ea-1f1fa | OPPORTUNITY CARD | 1f50e Search for a job in Germany | 1f4c5 Valid for up to 12 months | 1f4bc For skilled workers
chidi (shock): A whole year to find a job?
quddus (thumbs): Up to twelve months. But it can't be extended, so you need to use that time well.

== office | NEXT DAY · OFFICE | modern office with a world map, plants and a laptop | desk @chidi
chidi (think): Who qualifies?
quddus (talk): Either your degree or vocational qualification is fully recognised in Germany, or you collect enough points from things like education, work experience, language, and age.
> 2705 | THE BASICS | 1f393 Recognised qualification, or | 1f4ca Enough points (education, work, language) | 1f4b0 Proof you can support yourself
chidi (worried): And money?
quddus (point): You must show you can support yourself while you search, for example with a blocked account. Check the exact amount on the official Make it in Germany site.
chidi (cheer): Guten Tag, Germany! I'm doing my research first!
